**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

Decision 0001 merged reports on subject alone. #4471 shows the cost: 412 reports with similar
subjects were merged into one ticket, but they come from two causes. Reports with the same
subject need not share a bug (see [#4471 split](/kb/incidents/4471-split)).

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they share a cause: the tenant's locale and booking form,
and the way the report came in (`causeOf` in `causes.ts`). The desk merges on cause, not on subject.

## Consequences

- Each ticket carries one cause and a count of the reports it covers.
- Reports read differently from their cause stay under the cause and get a footnote.
- Merging takes one lookup of the tenant, not a read of the body.

